\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Where each stopping condition attaches to the pipeline.} A request moves through authority and contract check (stops 1--2: uncertain authority or an invalid approval binding), evidence assembly and classification (stops 3, 5: an unresolved conflict or insufficient evidence), bounded draft generation by the planning assistant (stops 4, 7: prohibited content or an exhausted budget), deterministic then semantic verification (stop 6: a critical unsupported claim, boundary violation, or contradiction identified by either check), and a named human review gate, which rejects, revises, or escalates rather than triggering a numbered stop, before a signed handoff package is produced. Platform stages are deterministic; dashed stages are mediated by the bounded planning assistant, which holds no approval authority at any stage.}}{6}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:stop}{{4}{6}{\textbf {Where each stopping condition attaches to the pipeline.} A request moves through authority and contract check (stops 1--2: uncertain authority or an invalid approval binding), evidence assembly and classification (stops 3, 5: an unresolved conflict or insufficient evidence), bounded draft generation by the planning assistant (stops 4, 7: prohibited content or an exhausted budget), deterministic then semantic verification (stop 6: a critical unsupported claim, boundary violation, or contradiction identified by either check), and a named human review gate, which rejects, revises, or escalates rather than triggering a numbered stop, before a signed handoff package is produced. Platform stages are deterministic; dashed stages are mediated by the bounded planning assistant, which holds no approval authority at any stage}{figure.caption.5}{}}
