\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Probe-suite results by category.} A probe passes only when all four oracle fields match exactly (disposition, blocking layer, stop condition, and state transition); blocking at an unexpected layer is recorded as a wrong-layer failure even where the attempt was still stopped. \textit  {Boundary held} is passed plus wrong layer: the share of probes where the platform stopped or permitted the request appropriately, whether or not the specific mechanism matched the oracle's prediction. Not blocked is the only outcome that reflects a safety-relevant miss. Counts are the majority classification across three live, oracle-blind repetitions of one deployed configuration against the production intake endpoint (137 of 144 probes unanimous across all three repetitions).}}{9}{table.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:proberesults}{{2}{9}{\textbf {Probe-suite results by category.} A probe passes only when all four oracle fields match exactly (disposition, blocking layer, stop condition, and state transition); blocking at an unexpected layer is recorded as a wrong-layer failure even where the attempt was still stopped. \textit {Boundary held} is passed plus wrong layer: the share of probes where the platform stopped or permitted the request appropriately, whether or not the specific mechanism matched the oracle's prediction. Not blocked is the only outcome that reflects a safety-relevant miss. Counts are the majority classification across three live, oracle-blind repetitions of one deployed configuration against the production intake endpoint (137 of 144 probes unanimous across all three repetitions)}{table.caption.7}{}}
